   "text": "I read this as a cyclic peptide: Ac\u2011Nle\u2011cyclo[Glu\u2011His\u20112Nal\u2011Arg\u2011Trp\u2011NH\u2011(CH2)4\u2011NH\u2011], where the Glu side\u2011chain carboxyl is joined as an amide to a 1,4\u2011diaminobutane linker. The other end of that linker is amidated to the Trp C\u2011terminus, which closes the ring.\n\nResidue by residue:\n- **N\u2011terminus:** an acetyl group on a norleucine (n\u2011butyl side chain).\n- **Glu:** its side chain CH2CH2C(=O) forms the amide to the linker NH.\n- **His:** a 4\u2011substituted imidazole with an NH.\n- **2\u2011Naphthylalanine:** the side chain is a CH2 on the 2\u2011position of naphthalene.\n- **Arg:** a three\u2011carbon chain ending in a guanidine.\n- **Trp:** a 3\u2011indolylmethyl side chain, with its C\u2011terminal C(=O) bonded to the NH(CH2)4NH linker.\n\nStereochemistry: I assigned each centre from the wedge bond to its side chain, with the implicit H pointing back. This gave D\u2011Nle, L\u2011Glu, D\u2011His, D\u20112Nal, D\u2011Arg and D\u2011Trp. The mix is unusual for this kind of peptide (a ligand of this type would normally have L residues apart from D\u20112Nal), but I followed the drawing as I read it. I could not confirm from the image whether any wedge is actually hashed.\n\nSMILES: CC(=O)N[C@H](CCCC)C(=O)N[C@H]1CCC(=O)NCCCCNC(=O)[C@@H](Cc2c[nH]c3ccccc23)NC(=O)[C@@H](CCCNC(=N)N)NC(=O)[C@@H](Cc2ccc3ccccc3c2)NC(=O)[C@@H](Cc2c[nH]cn2)NC1=O"
